{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at `66f7b0eb3c0be4a85ffdb9f96579ebddfaba6a41`, tree `34393fe0`. Cards and receipts now name the signer from signed records, and the failed gate plus its follow-up meet `docs/testing.md`. One claim in the note has no witness, and I name it below. It fails safely, so it does not block.\n\n**What I checked.** I read the note and the full source diff apart from `generated.ts`. At this head I ran `security-entry-points.test.mjs` (10 pass), `s4.test.mjs` (24 pass), `view-sessions.test.ts` (17 pass), and the new native case in `change-view.scope.test.ts`, and the worktree stays clean. The manifest hash matches. All 199 files in the four units match their hashes, all 21 table digests name manifest entries, each unit's checksums pass, and no file is writable. My text scan for link, key, JWT and bearer patterns found nothing.\n\n**The failed gate and its follow-up: conditions met.** `gate.exit` reads exit 1, and the log names the stale `service.ts:$module` seal. Counting, plain and native were unreached.\n- `git diff 401853e5 19da8139` names only `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs`, and the diff changes two seal literals and adds their comments.\n- No file imports it. `scripts/test.mjs:15` lists its path as a string, and `usage-report.mjs` imports a different file.\n- `followup.exit` and `native.exit` read exit 0: the owning file passes 10, Counting 56, plain 3556 with 1 skip, native 1029 with 2 skips. Those totals match the retained extracts. `gate.sh` has no step after `test`.\n- A `.mjs` test feeds no compiler context.\n\nI read the `McpService` diff myself before accepting the new seals. It adds one private `WeakMap`, one `signerOf` port, and `#withSigner` on the results of send and settle, after their existing gates. It adds no route, tool, or authority. The original gate stays failed, and the note says so.\n\n**Card workflow.** Run 41397945887 reports success at `401853e5`, and its log reads `{\"cases\":82,...,\"errors\":[]}`. The script runs the native witness first, then replays its displays. The inputs stay the same through the repair by the diff above.\n\n**Attribution follows the signed record.**\n- `Collection.signer` reads the pinned entry, checks its scope and hash, and takes `signed.intent.actor`. A wrong hash throws, and the list and change paths catch it and say the signer is unavailable.\n- `actSigner` needs one active key, one active member, a supported kind, the same membership, and for an agent one active person as controller. `view-sessions.test.ts` covers a removed controller, another membership, and a revoked key.\n- The native witness uses a different reviewer from the author, and it checks the chip, the receipt, the context receipt, the signed key, and the receipt after refresh, for all three kinds. `native-agent-320-receipt.png` shows the agent's chip with its controller above a receipt naming @check, unclipped at width 320.\n- Both controls report DISTINGUISHES on their named assertions.\n\n**Architecture: sound.** The signer stays out of public tool results: `cardSigner` appears only with a card position, and the `context` and change tools strip `signer`. The golden's only changes are card reasons and the question's chip.\n\n**Security: no new authority.** The chip and receipt are display only. Names reach the card through a text node, and the browser supplies no part of the signer. The public key shows only when no member resolves. Raw native output with bearer-shaped test values stays out of the unit, and the note says so.\n\n**Simplification: nothing to remove.**\n\n**Items.**\n\n1. **Needs You and Work chips have no witness. The builder adds one at the next edit of `change-view.scope.test.ts`.** The note says those cards name the selected record's opening act. I found no test that asserts \"Opening act signed by\" with a real signer, and the golden holds only the \"unavailable\" line, from fixtures with no opening entry. `witness 1` shows that `openingSigner` works for a change's manifest, so I expect the list path to work. Nothing shows it. If it fails, each list card says that the signer is unavailable, which is true but is not what `c6ced04f` asks for. One native assertion on `view_needs_you` closes this.\n2. **Card-path rule (planner).** This head adds `packages/mcp/test/support/actor-cards.ts` and `packages/mcp/test/change-view.scope.test.ts` to the workflow's paths. Rule `0998f9ec` should name them too. The browser script now runs a native case that also depends on `packages/mcp/src/service.ts`, and that path is not in the workflow's list, so a change to the receipt's signer there would not trigger the run. The planner decides whether to add it.\n\n**How far this goes.** Native scopes with `OwnGit`, `WorkspaceStandIn`, and a test clock, then a browser replay. No deployed host, no desktop AI app, and no person. The stream and Goose limits keep their owners, as the note says.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:88746d3aa2439e60c96129e812e3c4ddabdbfdec","binding":"assigned","head":"66f7b0eb3c0be4a85ffdb9f96579ebddfaba6a41","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:391275da7611dcac1995dd0a4539fa00d514f1aa\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:627dd5ffc7363faac8bad02e69ed03075d2ac22a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:391275da7611dcac1995dd0a4539fa00d514f1aa","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}